    description: "Per aggregate-v5 prospector signal (2026-04-11 run, 2441 candidates in python_orm_dispatch category): Django ORM method calls via QuerySet/Manager (e.g. MyModel.objects.filter(), MyModel.objects.get(), instance.save()) are not resolved to the Model class definitions that provide the fields/methods being accessed. This produces dead-code-maybe false positives where Model methods appear unused because the callers go through the QuerySet/Manager proxy.\n\nScope: audit existing packages/hypergumbo-lang-python/src/hypergumbo_lang_python/orm.py (which already handles some SQLAlchemy/ORM patterns per agent note 'likely fits inside existing orm.py'). Extend to capture Django's QuerySet/Manager -> Model method resolution. Emit uses edges from the call site to Model method definitions so dispatch is visible in the graph.\n\nSuccess criterion: re-run dead-code-prospector aggregate and verify python_orm_dispatch count drops meaningfully below 2441.\n\nSource: WI-tubot aggregate-v5 analysis, 2026-04-16T19:25:09Z discussion entry."  # 0749
